<Project>
  <!--
    Shared build configuration for every test project.

    src/Directory.Build.props does not reach tests/ (MSBuild stops at the first Directory.Build.props
    it finds walking up from the project directory), so test code used to compile without
    warnings-as-errors while production code did not. The documented gate is "warnings are errors"
    for the whole solution, and CI builds src/Cinomni.slnx with -warnaserror, which includes every
    test project. This file makes the local build and the CI build agree.

    It mirrors src/Directory.Build.props property for property with ONE deliberate exception:
    InvariantGlobalization. src/Directory.Build.props sets it, so the Host ships without ICU while
    these test assemblies run with it, and a culture-aware or Unicode-aware operation can therefore
    behave one way in a passing test and another way in the shipped process.

    That is not hypothetical, which is why the property is not simply copied here. Under invariant
    globalization string.Normalize(NormalizationForm.FormD) returns the string unchanged, so
    Cinomni.ReleaseParsing's TitleAnalyzer.NormalizeTitle does not fold diacritics in the Host:
    "Amélie" and "Amelie" produce different canonical keys in production, and
    ReleaseParserTests.Diacritics_are_folded_so_the_canonical_key_collapses_across_indexers passes
    only because ICU is present here. Setting the property would turn that test red without fixing
    the parser, and the fix changes canonical keys that are already persisted, which is a
    ReleaseParsing decision (a parse rule version), not a build-configuration one.

    So: aligning the two is the goal, the parser has to move first, and until it does this comment
    is the record of why they differ instead of an accident nobody noticed.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
